+	 * Serialize against filemap faults as well as truncation.  Merely
+	 * scanning the page cache can race a MAP_PRIVATE fault which inserts a
+	 * stale page immediately after the scan.  The ordered sequence is not
+	 * published until the exact size and complete data invalidation have
+	 * both succeeded.
+	 *
+	 * This lock is the whole cached-data coherence argument, not an
+	 * optimisation.  Every path that can insert a folio into a SHARED
+	 * mapping -- filemap_create_folio(), page_cache_ra_unbounded(),
+	 * filemap_fault() -- holds mapping->invalidate_lock shared across the
+	 * FUSE READ it issues, or holds the folio locked across an asynchronous
+	 * read-ahead read that was started under it.  Taking the lock
+	 * exclusively here therefore partitions every fill: one that began
+	 * before the authority applied finishes and is removed below, and one
+	 * that begins after this unlock necessarily fetches post-apply bytes.
+	 *
+	 * The withdrawal is by ordered sequence, never by size delta.  A
+	 * same-length overwrite arrives with a strictly greater sequence and
+	 * reaches invalidate_inode_pages2() exactly like a grow or a shrink;
+	 * only a replayed or already-installed sequence returns early above.
+	 * truncate_pagecache() therefore does the tail work of a shrink, and
+	 * invalidate_inode_pages2() does the actual data withdrawal -- including
+	 * unmapping any MAP_PRIVATE page tables that reference the old bytes.
